  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Eren, Mikasa, and Armin are playing a game with an array AAA of length NNN to get FREEDOM.\n\nEren can select any indices iii and jjj such that 1≤i&lt;j≤N1\\le i\\lt j\\le N1≤i&lt;j≤N.\n\nLet a,b,a, b,a,b, and ccc denote the points of Eren, Mikasa, and Armin respectively, where:\n\n\na=Ai−Aja = A_i - A_ja=Ai​−Aj​\nb=Ai+Ajb = A_i + A_jb=Ai​+Aj​\nc=Ai×Ajc = A_i \\times A_jc=Ai​×Aj​\nEren, Mikasa and Armin will get FREEDOM if the values of a,b,a, b,a,b, and ccc form an arithmetic progression.\n\nThe task is to count the number of ways Eren can select pairs (i,j)(i, j)(i,j) such that they get FREEDOM.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN — the number of elements in the array.\nThe second line of each test case contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1,A_2,\\ldots ,A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ — the elements of the array.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line, the number of pairs (i,j)(i, j)(i,j) such that Eren, Mikasa and Armin get FREEDOM.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1031 \\leq T \\leq 10^31≤T≤103",
      "1≤N≤1051 \\leq N \\leq 10^51≤N≤105",
      "1≤Ai≤1091 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^91≤Ai​≤109",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 5⋅1055\\cdot 10^55⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
